            0.119
          ],
          "content": "40"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.138,
            0.607,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, their product $= \\left( x - 5 \\right) \\left( 40 - x \\right)$ $= 40x - x^{2} - 200 + 5x$ $= -x^{2} + 45x - 200$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.214,
            0.77,
            0.234
          ],
          "content": "So, $-x^{2}+45x-200=124$ (Given that product = 124)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.239,
            0.433,
            0.258
          ],
          "content": "i.e., $-x^{2}+45x-324=0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.264,
            0.433,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": "i.e., $x^{2}-45x+324=0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.291,
            0.868,
            0.309
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the number of marbles John had, satisfies the quadratic equation"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.322,
            0.315,
            0.514,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": "x^{2}-45x+324=0",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.341,
            0.793,
            0.36
          ],
          "content": "which is the required representation of the problem mathematically."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.366,
            0.633,
            0.385
          ],
          "content": "(ii) Let the number of toys produced on that day be x."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.391,
            0.858,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the cost of production (in rupees) of each toy that day = 55 – x So, the total cost of production (in rupees) that day $x \\left( 55 - x \\right)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.441,
            0.257,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.368,
            0.441,
            0.537,
            0.461
          ],
          "content": "x \\left( 55 - x \\right) = 750",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.467,
            0.19,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.383,
            0.466,
            0.536,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": "55x - x^{2} = 750",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.492,
            0.19,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.305,
            0.492,
            0.515,
            0.511
          ],
          "content": "-x^{2}+55x-750=0",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.518,
            0.19,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.324,
            0.516,
            0.514,
            0.535
          ],
          "content": "x^{2}-55x+750=0",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.542,
            0.901,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the number of toys produced that day satisfies the quadratic equation"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.319,
            0.567,
            0.515,
            0.586
          ],
          "content": "x^{2}-55x+750=0",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_20.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.593,
            0.791,
            0.612
          ],
          "content": "which is the required representation of the problem mathematically."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.625,
            0.742,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": "**Example 2 :** Check whether the following are quadratic equations:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.239,
            0.65,
            0.474,
            0.668
          ],
          "content": "(i) $(x - 2)^{2} \\pm \\underline{1} = 2x - 3$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.567,
            0.65,
            0.885,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": "(ii) $x(x + 1) + 8 = (x + 2)(x - 2)$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.231,
            0.682,
            0.453,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": "x(2x + 3) = x^{2} + 1",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_25.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.561,
            0.683,
            0.766,
            0.702
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{(iv)} \\left(x + 2\\right)^{3} = x^{3} - 4",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_26.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.715,
            0.205,
            0.733
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Solution :"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.741,
            0.622,
            0.761
          ],
          "content": "(i) $\\mathrm{LHS} = (x - 2)^2 + 1 = x^2 - 4x + 4 + 1 = x^2 - 4x + 5$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.135,
            0.776,
            0.629,
            0.795
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, $(x - 2)^{2} + 1 = 2x - 3$ can be rewritten as"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.358,
            0.803,
            0.563,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": "x^{2}-4x+5=2x-3",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_30.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.83,
            0.191,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.36,
            0.828,
            0.517,
            0.846
          ],
          "content": "x^{2}-6x+8=0",
          "image_source": "images/page_2_equation_32.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.855,
            0.473,
            0.872
          ],
          "content": "It is of the form $ax^{2}+bx+c=0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.967,
            0.563,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.88,
            0.659,
            0.899
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the given equation is a quadratic equation."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
